>> title: Ham Sui Gok
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: pork, glutinous rice, chinese, deep-fry, dumpling
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: hom sui gok, haam seui gok, 鹹水角, fried pork dumpling, football dumpling, salty water dumpling
>> servings: 16
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the oil starts at 300°F and is eased up; dropped into hot oil the dough browns before it puffs and never blisters

>> step: fry the pork and shrimp 5 min, cool 20 min
Fry @ground pork{8%oz}(225 g) with @dried shrimp{2%Tbs}(soaked and chopped), @dried shiitake mushrooms{2}(soaked and diced), @scallions{2}(sliced), @oyster sauce{1%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{2%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp}, @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} and @cornstarch{1%tsp}(slaked in 1 Tbs water) in a #wok{} for ~fry{5%min}, then spread it on a tray and ~cool{20%min}.

>> step: scald the wheat starch, knead the dough, rest 20 min
Stir @boiling water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) into @wheat starch{1/4%cup}(30 g) to a paste, then knead it together with @glutinous rice flour{2%cups}(280 g), @sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g), @lard{3%Tbs} and @warm water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) to a dough like soft putty and ~rest{20%min}.

>> step: shape 16 footballs around the filling
Shape @&(~1)dough{} into 16 balls, flatten each one, close @&(~2)filling{} inside and work it into a pointed football between your palms.

>> step: fry 300°F (150°C) 6 min, easing the heat up
Fry @&(~1)dumplings{} in @peanut oil{6%cups}(1.4 L; started at 300°F/150°C) for ~fry{6%min}, easing the heat up as they take colour, until they are blistered and deep gold.
